## Do these two things and the next run publishes everything

### 1. Make the token reachable (30 seconds)

`publish.sh` resolves the PAT to `$(dirname REPO_DIR)/.fly-connectome-gh-token`.
Only `/Users/rj/personal/fly-connectome-videos` is attached to the task, so inside the
sandbox that resolves to `$HOME/mnt/.fly-connectome-gh-token` — outside every mounted
folder. If the token exists at `/Users/rj/personal/.fly-connectome-gh-token`, the
session cannot see it and never will.

On your Mac:

```bash
cd /Users/rj/personal/fly-connectome-videos
mv ../.fly-connectome-gh-token .fly-connectome-gh-token   # already in .gitignore
```

Then add `FLY_TOKEN_FILE="$REPO_DIR/.fly-connectome-gh-token"` as the default in
`publish.sh`, or attach `/Users/rj/personal` to the scheduled task as a second folder.

### 2. Confirm the GitHub repo and Pages

`github.com/honicky/fly-connectome-videos` → **404 unauthenticated.** That is what a
*private* repo returns too, so this is **not** proof it is missing. Earlier notes in the
history file overclaimed here; it is genuinely undecidable without a credential, and a
scheduled run has none.

`https://honicky.github.io/fly-connectome-videos/` → **404**, confirmed 2026-10-08 from
the cloud container (working egress, not the proxy-refused curl earlier runs tried).
So Pages is not serving. If the site is meant to be public, the repo must be public —
private-repo Pages requires a paid plan and serves privately.

So: create the repo if it does not exist, enable Pages on `main`, and note here which it was.

### 3. Then write `publish.sh pull` / `push` — it does not exist

`COLLECTING.md` section 6 and the task prompt both call `publish.sh pull` and
`publish.sh push`. **The script takes no arguments.** `grep -E '\$1|case|getopts'` finds
nothing; the only `push` in it is the `git push` on line 44. It runs `build.py` then
`git status` in its own directory — the mounted mirror, which has no `.git` — and dies
under `set -e` even with a valid token. The `$HOME/fly-work` flow the runbook documents
was never implemented.

Left unwritten deliberately, in 11 runs: it cannot be tested from a scheduled session
(no repo to clone, no token to push with), and shipping an untested `git push` into an
unattended daily job is how a backlog becomes a clobbered repo. ~10 minutes once 1 and 2
are done. Git genuinely cannot run inside the mounted folder — the sandbox blocks file
deletion, so git's lock files survive and every commit after the first dies with
`cannot lock ref 'HEAD': File exists`. That part of the runbook is correct.

> **Clobber hazard — read before writing the mirror-back step.**
> `data/pending-merge.json` is the only copy of the entire backlog, is **not** gitignored,
> and GitHub currently holds nothing. If `pull`/`push` mirror a clone of an empty repo back
> over the mounted folder, **the whole backlog is destroyed in one run.** Either commit it
> in the very first push, or make mirror-back copy only `index.html` and `data/items.json`.

